//~ CHECK-ONLY
// ir: the type table and the checked IR of stage1 (contracts/checked-ir.md). It imports no part of
// the front end, so the back end and the prover use it alone.
//
// Modules:
//   types      the type table: one `TypeKey` row per type (the front end's and the IR's)
//   features   the target feature table
//   model      the module as flat columns
//   bytes      numbers, quoting, paths, target names in text
//   grammar    the generated IR text tables (`generated.ir_text_*`)
//   lexer      the lexer of one line
//   drive      the LL(1) driver of one line, with the syntax messages
//   stage      step 1: each line into staged rows
//   read       step 2 and the module build; `read.read` runs steps 1 and 2
//   verify     step 3: the verifier of untrusted modules (`vtypes`: what it knows of types)
//   load       steps 1 to 3
//   print      the printer
//   known      the compiler-known items (`generated.known_items`)
//   generated.opt_table  the release optimizer's limits, weights, and op rows (opt.toml)
//   errs       the faults of an input and their rendering
//   umap       a u64 -> u32 map for per-fn numbering
